TI  - [Successful risk management in flexible bronchoscopy].
PG  - 2346-50
LID - 10.1055/s-0029-1242692 [doi]
AB  - Flexible bronchoscopy is one of the most important diagnostic procedures in 
      respiratory medicine. The investigator operates in a vital organ and therefore 
      must face a broad range of potential complications. This article provides an 
      overview of all important complications associated with flexible bronchoscopy. It 
      is further discussed how this risk can be minimized. A skillfull team, close 
      monitoring and readily available resuscitation facilities are mandatory to avoid 
      and to deal with major complications.
