TI  - [Postoperative complications in thoracic surgery. Special aspects].
PG  - 807-13
LID - 10.1007/s00104-009-1688-x [doi]
AB  - Complications are quite common in thoracic surgery due to the comorbidities of 
      the mostly elderly patients and to the fact that the surgical procedure itself 
      compromises the respiratory apparatus. Consequently, pneumonia and respiratory 
      failure represent the most common causes of death. Postoperatively, early 
      diagnosis and treatment of these complications are paramount while most other 
      events can be anticipated and thus be avoided with corresponding operative 
      experience.
