TI  - Endobronchial schwannoma presenting with bronchial obstruction.
PG  - 133-4
LID - 10.1510/icvts.2009.215103 [doi]
AB  - Schwannomas are relatively uncommon, benign nerve sheath tumors. Thoracic 
      schwannomas most often appear in the posterior mediastinum. Pulmonary schwannomas 
      are exceedingly rare and can present a diagnostic challenge. We present a case of 
      an endobronchial schwannoma presenting with bronchial obstruction and review the 
      literature of this unusual entity.
