TI  - The Lady Windermere syndrome.
PG  - 334-6
LID - 10.4104/pcrj.2009.00019 [doi]
AB  - Lady Windermere syndrome is right middle lobe or lingular segment bronchiectasis 
      due to Mycobacterium avium intracellulare infection. In this brief report we 
      describe two cases with contrasting clinical courses and discuss controversies 
      regarding aetiology, pathogenesis and treatment. Hypotheses explaining middle 
      lobe predilection are discussed and an alternative hypothesis is offered.
