TI  - [ACTH-dependent Cushing syndrome, a diagnostic challenge].
PG  - 205-8
LID - 10.1016/S1575-0922(09)70986-6 [doi]
AB  - ACTH dependent Cushing syndrome accounts for approximately 80% of all Cushing 
      syndrome. Distinguishing the pituitary origin from ectopic one is still a 
      diagnosis problem in some cases, especially in bronchial carcinoids, because 
      approximately 50% show cortisol suppresion after dexametasone and may be small 
      and, therefore, difficult to detect in chest radiography. We present a case of a 
      patient with ACTH dependent Cushing syndrome of difficult localization with usual 
      diagnosis tests.
