TI  - Treatment of heterogeneous emphysema using the spiration IBV valves.
PG  - 247-53, ix-x
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2009.02.005 [doi]
AB  - Ninety-eight emphysema patients were treated at 13 international sites during a 
      3-year series of single-arm, open-label studies with the IBV valve and a 
      multi-lobar treatment approach. Fifty six percent of subjects had a clinically 
      meaningful improvement in health-related quality of life, but standard pulmonary 
      function and exercise studies were insensitive effectiveness measures. 
      Quantitative CT analyses of regional lung changes showed lobar volume changes in 
      over 85% of subjects. Lung volume reduction was an uncommon mechanism for a 
      treatment response with bilateral upper lobe treatment. A redirection of inspired 
      air, an interlobar shift to health-ier lung tissue, was the most common mechanism 
      for a valve treatment response.
