TI  - Slide tracheoplasty as a rescue technique after unsuccessful patch tracheoplasty.
PG  - 1029-31
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2009.01.024 [doi]
AB  - Long-segment tracheal stenosis with complete tracheal rings is a severe and 
      life-threatening problem in small children. Slide tracheoplasty has largely 
      become the treatment of choice for these patients. Its use after the failure of 
      other techniques has not been previously reported. We describe a 3-year-old child 
      who underwent a rescue slide tracheoplasty for re-stenosis after initial patch 
      tracheoplasty for long-segment tracheal stenosis and pulmonary artery sling.
