TI  - Complete tracheal duplication in an adult with thoracic aortic coarctation.
PG  - 138-41
LID - 10.1097/RTI.0b013e3181901760 [doi]
AB  - Partial and complete duplication of the trachea have previously been reported as 
      rare causes of respiratory distress in children. We report a case of complete 
      tracheal duplication detected incidentally in an adult during a computed 
      tomography angiogram of the heart performed as part of an evaluation for 
      coarctation of the aorta.
