TI  - Solitary lung metastasis diagnosed 30 years after surgery for thyroid cancer.
PG  - 2016-7
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2009.04.134 [doi]
AB  - A 75-year-old woman with a history of extrapulmonary malignancies (ie, thyroid 
      cancer and colon cancer) underwent a lobectomy for a solitary nodule in the left 
      lung. Pathologic examination showed a lung metastasis from papillary thyroid 
      cancer treated 30 years earlier. Solitary metastasis to the lung from thyroid 
      cancer is unusual, and our case presented the long interval from initial 
      treatment to the identification of metastasis. A careful follow-up is mandatory, 
      and one should keep in mind the delayed metastasis in the patient with 
      differentiated thyroid cancer.
