DP  - 2009 Jun
TI  - Management of the difficult pediatric airway: efficacy of airway exchange 
      catheters with rigid bronchoscopy.
PG  - 964-6
AB  - The airway exchange catheter can be used both to ventilate the lungs and to act 
      as a guide for reintubation in patients of all ages who have a tenuous airway. We 
      report the case of a 2-year-old boy with an anatomically challenging airway in 
      whom both an airway exchange catheter and a rigid bronchoscope were used to 
      visualize and maintain a secure airway. We also review the literature as it 
      pertains to the management of the difficult pediatric airway.
