TI  - Successful emergent reintubation using the Aintree intubation catheter and a 
      laryngeal mask airway.
PG  - 148-50
AB  - Tracheal extubation can be potentially catastrophic, especially in patients with 
      difficult airways. This article describes a case where planned extubation in a 
      patient with a large tongue lesion led to complete airway obstruction and 
      subsequent cardiac arrest. Reintubation was facilitated using a laryngeal mask 
      airway and an Aintree intubation catheter.
