AB  - The authors report a case of pulmonary arteriovenous malformation in a 
      48-year-old man. The bronchoscopy revealed a fragile lingular tumoral formation. 
      The diagnosis was based on the thoracotomy and the histopathological findings. 
      The endoscopic features and the different diagnostic options of pulmonary 
      arteriovenous malformation are discussed.
