VI  - 37
IP  - 2
DP  - 2010 Apr
TI  - Surgical treatment of primary tracheal dyskinesia in a 14-month-old child--case 
      report.
PG  - 263-7
LID - 10.1016/j.anl.2009.06.012 [doi]
AB  - The primary form of tracheal dyskinesia in early childhood is a rare congenital 
      malformation of unknown origin. The degree of the posterior membranous tracheal 
      wall involvement determines the intensity of obstruction and the severity of the 
      clinical picture. The aim of this paper is to present a case of a 14-month-old 
      child with severe tracheal dyskinesia that required surgical treatment. Fascia 
      lata graft fixated with fibrin glue was used in strengthening the posterior 
      tracheal wall. Three years following the surgery, the child is without breathing 
      difficulties. In severe cases of primary dyskinesia, surgical treatment using 
      fascia lata graft, fixated with fibrin glue is recommended in strengthening the 
      posterior tracheal wall.
