DP  - 2009 Oct
TI  - Closure of pneumonectomy stump fistula using custom Y and cuff-link-shaped 
      silicone prostheses.
PG  - 339-42
AB  - Large postpneumonectomy stump fistulas pose a significant problem for thoracic 
      surgeons and interventional bronchoscopists. We present a case of successful 
      rigid bronchoscopic repair of a complete right pneumonectomy stump dehiscence 
      using a custom-built stent made of a sculpted silicone Y stent sutured to a new 
      cuff-link-shaped DJ-Fistula stent. This resulted in rapid symptom resolution, 
      weaning from mechanical ventilation and discharge home in a patient with 
      bronchogenic carcinoma, respiratory failure, and significant other comorbidities 
      that precluded repeat thoracotomy.
