TI  - Pleomorphic adenoma of the main bronchus in an adult treated using a wedge 
      bronchiectomy.
PG  - 43-5
LID - 10.1007/s11748-008-0319-7 [doi]
AB  - A 34-year-old woman had complained of dyspnea on exertion for 3 months and was 
      found to have a volume loss of the left lung. A smooth, vascularized, whitish 
      nodular mass obstructing the orifice of the left main bronchus was noted on 
      bronchoscopy. We performed a deep wedge resection of the main bronchus, 
      preserving the lung parenchyma. Histopathologically, the tumor specimen was 
      compatible with pleomorphic adenoma. To our knowledge, only two cases of 
      pleomorphic adenoma arising from the main bronchus have been reported in the 
      English-language literature, and ours is the first report of lung-preserving 
      surgery.
