TI  - Nonmedical therapy for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.
PG  - 137-45
LID - 10.1513/pats.200809-114GO [doi]
AB  - Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) is a category of diseases with 
      chronic airflow obstruction and hyperinflation. The GOLD committee and the 
      American Thoracic Society/European Respiratory Society have published detailed, 
      evidence-based reviews of management, providing stepped-care algorithms for 
      pharmacologic and nonpharmacologic therapy. Over the past several decades, this 
      has led to numerous nonpharmacologic approaches to ameliorate symptoms in these 
      patients.
