TI  - Bronchoscopy for foreign body removal: where is the delay?
PG  - 956-8
LID - S1806-37132008001100011 [pii]
AB  - This was a retrospective analysis of the medical charts of 145 patients treated 
      at the Bronchoscopy and Thoracic Surgery Clinic of the Hospital das Clínicas da 
      Universidade Estadual de Campinas (HC-Unicamp, State University of Campinas 
      Hospital das Clínicas) over a period of 10 years. There was a significant 
      difference related to the site of first medical visit (Unicamp-HC versus other 
      institutions) in terms of the time elapsed between the suspicion of bronchial 
      aspiration and the actual respiratory endoscopic examination. However, no 
      significant difference was found in the rate of positive results. The low number 
      of referral centers that provide emergency respiratory endoscopy can negatively 
      influence the treatment of patients under suspicion of bronchial aspiration, 
      jeopardizing the overall recovery in the mid- and long-term.
