TI  - [Atypically located pulmonary adenoid cystic carcinoma: case report].
PG  - 210-4
AB  - Pulmonary adenoid cystic carcinomas typically arise from central extra-pulmonary 
      airways and lung involvement is rare. On the other hand, this entity should be 
      kept in mind because it has a more favorable clinical course compared to the 
      primary lung adenocarcinoma. In this paper; the clinical, radiological and 
      pathological aspects of a 47 years old man with a complaint of chronic cough, who 
      was found to have a mass lesion at upper lobe of right lung and a final diagnosis 
      of primary pulmonary adenoid cystic carcinoma according to transbronchial needle 
      biopsy and pneumonectomy, was presented.
