TI  - Subcutaneous emphysema and pneumomediastinum due to foreign body aspiration.
PG  - 129-30
LID - 10.1055/s-2007-989485 [doi]
AB  - Pneumomediastinum is a result of perforation of the tracheobronchial tree. When 
      air enters the interstitial space, air diffuses along the perivascular sheaths 
      toward the mediastinum. If an air leak persists, subcutaneous emphysema occurs 
      owing to the continuous leakage of air. Foreign body aspiration rarely causes 
      pneumomediastinum and subcutaneous emphysema. Removal of the foreign body results 
      in a resorption of air and the resolution of symptoms. Here, we present a rare 
      case of foreign body aspiration in a 2-year-old patient who presented with 
      pneumomediastinum and subcutaneous emphysema.
