TI  - Broncholithiasis: case report and discussion with focus on radiographic findings.
PG  - 22-3
AB  - Broncholithiasis is a condition arising when calcified material in the form of a 
      stone or stones is found in the bronchial lumen. Some authors have included the 
      impingement of a calcified peri-bronchial lymph node on the external surface of a 
      bronchus, as part of the definition. The incidence of broncholithiasis has 
      dwindled in recent years, possibly as a result of the reduced incidence of 
      tuberculosis. Despite this it remains a condition with potentially serious 
      complications, which needs to be diagnosed and treated effectively. Here, the 
      case of a 71 year old man with broncholithiasis is discussed.
