TI  - [Palliative measures in lung cancer].
PG  - 32-4
AB  - A patient in the final stages of lung cancer primarily needs effective pain 
      management, treatment of symptoms such as coughing, breathing difficulty, fatigue 
      and if necessary, relief through anti-metastasis therapy when a curative therapy 
      is no longer useful. After all best possible medical measures have been employed, 
      the final tasks of the family physician include speaking and listening to the 
      patient, ideally without time pressure, and providing supportive information for 
      the patient and his family.
