TI  - A case of plastic bronchitis presenting 9 years after Fontan.
PG  - 157-9
AB  - A 15-year-old boy with hypoplastic left heart syndrome experienced plastic 
      bronchitis 9 years after completion of a nonfenestrated lateral tunnel Fontan. 
      Despite cardiac catheterization with coil embolization of collateral vessels and 
      initiation of a pulmonary toilet regimen, including aerosolized tissue 
      plasminogen activator, he continued to expectorate large acellular-mucinous 
      casts. Finally, after optimization of cardiac function with the addition of 
      carvedilol, the expectorated casts decreased in number. This report reviews 
      pathophysiology of plastic bronchitis cast formation and therapy in the context 
      of this late presentation after Fontan.
