TI  - Treatment of bronchopleural fistula with small intestinal mucosa and fibrin glue 
      sealant.
PG  - 1383-6
AB  - Bronchopleural fistula can be a devastating complication of pulmonary resections. 
      Treatment options are often limited and carry significant morbidity or mortality, 
      or both. We present a case of bronchopleural fistula occurring after pulmonary 
      lobectomy for aspergilloma in a patient with recurrent acute lymphoblastic 
      leukemia. The bronchopleural fistula was treated using bronchoscopic obliteration 
      with Tisseel VH Fibrin Sealant (Baxter Healthcare Corp, Westlake Village, CA) and 
      small intestinal submucosa with complete resolution and no morbidity. The 
      relevant literature is reviewed.
