TI  - [Asymptomatic pulmonary actinomycosis diagnosed by transbronchial lung biopsy 
      (TBLB)].
PG  - 494-8
AB  - A 65-year-old asymptomatic man was admitted to our hospital because a chest 
      abnormal shadow had been pointed out on a medical examination. Our investigation 
      resulted that the consolidation in the left lung had been initially documented in 
      2002, and had been expanding every year. Bronchofiberscopy showed flare, swelling 
      and stenosis of the left B8, B9 and B10. Because the biopsy specimen from the B9 
      showed a mass of bacteria and surrounding granulation tissue, pulmonary 
      actinomycosis was diagnosed. Pulmonary actinomycosis should be considered in the 
      differential diagnosis of abnormal chest shadows regardless of the absence of 
      symptoms.
