TI  - Calcified endobronchial leiomyoma.
PG  - e91-3
AB  - We report a case of calcified endobronchial leiomyoma in the left main bronchus. 
      Leiomyoma of the airways is a rare benign tumour, usually described as a solitary 
      lesion and located in the membranous portion of the lower third of the trachea 
      and rarely in the bronchi. Chest CT showed a well-defined, calcified, polypoid 
      endobronchial mass with a broad stalk in the left main bronchus.
