TI  - Primary mediastinal synovial sarcoma.
PG  - 109-11
AB  - Synovial sarcoma occurs predominantly in the soft tissues of the extremities, but 
      is exceedingly rare in the mediastinum. It has overlapping histological and 
      immunophenotypic features with other tumours in the differential diagnosis. We 
      report a case of a patient who had an incidental finding of such a tumour. 
      Because of the rarity of this tumour in the mediastinum, optimal therapy is 
      unknown and the prognosis remains guarded.
