TI  - Bronchopleural fistula repair during Clagett closure utilizing a collagen matrix 
      plug.
PG  - 1519-21
AB  - We describe a 65-year-old man who was treated for an empyema after a right middle 
      and lower lobectomy for adenocarcinoma with a Clagett procedure who subsequently 
      had a bronchopleural fistula develop. After adequate debridement of the cavity 
      through dressing changes, the right bronchus intermedius bronchopleural fistula 
      was closed using a collagen porcine plug (Surgisis anal fistula plug [Cook 
      Medical Inc, Bloomington, IN]) placed through the cavity into the fistula along 
      with the placement of omentum into the cavity. This case report illustrates the 
      utility of collagen plugs to close bronchopleural fistulas.
