TI  - [Diagnosis of lung cancer. Image guided diagnostic endoscopy].
PG  - 16S28-16S35
AB  - The scope of fibreoptic bronchoscopy, which has a high sensitivity for biopsy of 
      visible bronchial lesions, has been extended to more difficult areas such as the 
      mediastinum and the periphery of the lung. This has become possible thanks to 
      technical developments in imaging including miniaturised ultrasound transducers, 
      electromagnetic guidance and positron emission tomography. These techniques which 
      are less invasive than mediastinoscopy or thoracotomy and are probably equally 
      cost-effective.
