TI  - Carcinoid tumor of lung with Cushing's syndrome.
PG  - 94-6
AB  - Carcinoid tumor of lung with Cushing's syndrome is a rare condition. We report a 
      38-year-old man, with a 28-month history of Cushing's syndrome presented with 
      hypertension, diabetes mellitus, decreased libido, muscle weakness and 
      fatigability, moon facies, buffalo hump, truncal obesity, cutaneous striae, and 
      easy bruisability. Diagnosis was made by measurements of ACTH (149 pg/mL) and 
      cortisol levels (36 microg/dL) and computerized tomography of the chest.
