AB  - Contralateral pneumothorax is potentially lethal in patients who have undergone 
      pneumonectomy. There are few reports about the diagnosis and treatment of this 
      situation. This is a report of our experience with selective lobar ventilation of 
      the middle and lower lobes using a guidewire and a bronchial blocker in the right 
      upper bronchus of a patient who had previously undergone left pneumonectomy.
