TI  - Tracheoinnominate fistula mimicking an endotracheal mass and rupture during rigid 
      bronchoscopy.
PG  - 1051-4
AB  - Bleeding from tracheoinnominate fistula is an uncommon, but life-threatening 
      complication, which typically arises when a tracheostomy tube erodes into the 
      posterior aspect of the innominate artery. However, it has never been reported as 
      a complication of rigid bronchoscopy. This study reviews the relevant literature 
      and explores the possibility of lethal tracheoinnominate fistula during these 
      procedures.
