TI  - Three cases of the nodular pulmonary amyloidosis with a longterm observation.
PG  - 283-6
AB  - Longterm observation with chest radiograph and computed tomography (CT) scan was 
      performed for pulmonary amyloidosis. There are few reports of primary pulmonary 
      amyloidosis with a longterm observation. We encountered three cases of nodular 
      pulmonary amyloidosis observed by intermittent chest radiograph or CT for 5 years 
      or more. The patients were a 54-year-old man, and 67- and 68-year old women. For 
      diagnosis, transbronchial biopsy and percutaneous lung biopsy were performed. 
      Amyloid nodules grew slowly and two cases showed findings of cavity and 
      calcification.
