AB  - Pulmonary artery catheterization is almost uniformly used nowadays in cardiac 
      surgery. Although rare, rupture of the pulmonary artery following catheterization 
      is highly lethal. This review examines ways of avoiding its occurrence and means 
      of improving outcomes in case of rupture.
