AB  - Pneumothoraces are sometimes complicated by a persistent air leak or 
      bronchopleural fistula requiring prolonged chest tube drainage. Non-surgical 
      treatment of persistent bronchopleural fistulas is often performed in patients 
      who are poor surgical candidates, but the ideal method of closure is not known. 
      Here we report closure of a persistent distal bronchopleural fistula using a 
      one-way endobronchial valve designed for the treatment of emphysema.
