TI  - Chronic lung abscess with Pasteurella multocida infection.
PG  - 754-6
AB  - We report a patient with chronic lung abscess due to Pasteurella multocida 
      infection that may be caused by the contact with cows in his workplace. Despite 
      its apparent rarity, chronic abscess due to P. multocida should be considered in 
      the differential diagnosis of solitary pulmonary masses. This case report 
      suggests that P. multocida infection can be potentially caused from saliva of 
      cows as well as dogs or cats.
