TI  - [Congenital bronchobiliary fistula detected by cholescintigraphy].
PG  - 216-8
AB  - A case of a six-year-old female patient diagnosed with congenital bronchobiliary 
      fistula is presented. Only 20 cases have been reported in the literature of this 
      disease in this institution. The patient showed signs and symptoms of a 
      respiratory illness from birth that complicated progressively. She was submitted 
      to multiple imaging studies like chest X rays, CT, ultrasound and Tc-99m HIDA 
      cholescintigraphy. This procedure confirmed the presence of a bronchobiliary 
      fistula that was corrected by surgery, with subsequent improvement of clinical 
      symptoms.
