TI  - Bronchial foreign bodies.
PG  - 849-52
AB  - Foreign body aspiration is an extremely serious problem in childhood with varied 
      clinical presentation demanding high degree of suspicion on the part of 
      clinician. Surgical emphysema of the neck and chest often complicates 
      tracheostomy and sharp penetrating injuries to the neck perforating viscera of 
      the aerodigestive tract. Rarely if follows chest injuries. But emphysema due to 
      the neck of foreign bodies in the bronchus is quite rare. The authors hereby 
      report four cases of surgical emphysema following foreign body aspiration into 
      the tracheobronchial tree.
