TI  - Tracheal stenting: a better method of dealing with airway obstruction due to 
      thyroid malignancies than tracheostomy.
PG  - 462-4
AB  - Tracheostomy remains the primary method of treatment of acute airway obstruction 
      due to malignant invasion and compression of the trachea. However, the 
      development of tracheal stents has provided an alternative effective treatment 
      modality. This case report and literature review highlights the benefits of 
      intra-luminal stenting, including resolution of distressing obstructive symptoms, 
      and subsequent improvement in quality of life.
