TI  - [A case of arteriovenous malformation seen as an endobronchial lesion].
PG  - 175-8
AB  - Pulmonary arteriovenous malformation (PAVM) is an abnormal communication between 
      pulmonary arteries and pulmonary veins, and congenital form is seen more 
      prevalently. The classic radiological appearance is a round, well-circumscribed 
      lesion. PAVM was observed in a 22-year-old male as an endobronchial lesion, and 
      treated by wedge resection. Reviewing the literature, we identified only one case 
      report that describes endobronchial view of PAVM.
