TI  - Endobronchial lipoma: a case report.
PG  - 432-5
AB  - Endobronchial lipoma (EL) is a rare benign neoplasm that may cause irreversible 
      pulmonary damage distally, and may be misdiagnosed clinically as a bronchial 
      carcinoid or malignant tumor. They simulate malignant tumors, because of the age, 
      sex and smoking history of the patients in whom they are found. Proper management 
      is a "must" in order to avoid serious and unnecessary complications of the lung. 
      We present a case of endobronchial lipoma, which is located in the right upper 
      lobe bronchus, and diagnosed and treated by surgery.
