TI  - Invasive pulmonary aspergillosis after renal transplantation treated by surgery.
PG  - 83-5
AB  - Invasive pulmonary aspergillosis is a serious complication in immunocompromised 
      patients. In those unresponsive to pharmacological treatment, or when drug 
      toxicity is excessive, surgery may resolve the condition. A 48-year-old woman 
      with invasive pulmonary aspergillosis after renal transplantation underwent 
      resection of the right upper lobe and the apical segment of the inferior lobe, 
      followed by complete recovery.
