DP  - 2003 Sep
TI  - Pulmonary mucormycosis presenting with recurrent laryngeal nerve palsy.
PG  - 912-3
AB  - Pulmonary mucormycosis is an uncommon infection and its endobronchial form is 
      rare. Fever, cough, dyspnoea and hemoptysis are the usual presenting symptoms. 
      Hoarseness of voice, a rare manifestation of endobronchial mucormycosis, has been 
      reported earlier but its exact anatomical basis was unclear. We report an 
      instance of polypoid endobronchial mucormycosis and vocal cord paralysis in a 
      patient with type I diabetes and diabetic ketoacidosis.
