TI  - Stridor in infants: diagnosis and management.
PG  - 255-64
AB  - Stridor is frequently encountered in the pediatric age group and can be alarming 
      to the parents. Many lesions and abnormalities can cause it and the challenge is 
      to pinpoint a specific diagnosis effectively. The patient is usually referred to 
      the pediatric otolaryngologist by the primary care physician who should be aware 
      of the different lesions to avoid any delay in proper management. In the 
      operating room, both the anesthesiologist and the surgeon should cooperate to 
      reach a proper diagnosis or in the extreme situation save the life of the baby.
