DP  - 2003 Apr
TI  - Repair of pulmonary artery sling by reimplantation without cardiopulmonary 
      bypass.
PG  - 101-3
AB  - A 20-month-old girl successfully underwent repair of pulmonary artery sling 
      through a median sternotomy by division of the left pulmonary artery and its 
      reimplantation into the main pulmonary artery without cardiopulmonary bypass or 
      tracheal reconstruction. The patient is doing well on 18 months follow-up with 
      unobstructed pulmonary blood flow and dramatic reduction of tracheal stenosis. 
      Simple repair of pulmonary artery sling is feasible with good results in selected 
      cases without tracheomalacia.
