TI  - Tracheomalacia and bronchomalacia in children: pathophysiology, assessment, 
      treatment and anaesthesia management.
PG  - 3-11
AB  - Tracheomalacia and bronchomalacia are becoming increasingly well recognized. 
      Although pathologically benign conditions, they are responsible for considerable 
      morbidity, occasional mortality and significant difficulties in the operating 
      theatre and intensive care unit. We performed an extensive literature search to 
      identify causal associations, methods of clinical and investigative assessment, 
      treatment modalities and anaesthetic experience with these conditions.
