DP  - 2001 Jun
TI  - Diagnostic techniques in paediatric tuberculosis.
PG  - 120-6
AB  - Accurate diagnosis of tuberculosis (TB) in children is crucial to provide 
      effective treatment and to identify the undiagnosed adult who probably infected 
      the child. The diagnosis of tuberculosis in children is often based only on 
      epidemiologic, clinical, and radiographic findings. Fibre-optic bronchoscopy may 
      also be helpful but the recovery of tuberculous bacilli, which establishes the 
      diagnosis, is difficult in children. Rapid diagnostic tests such as direct 
      amplification and serological tests have been developed to improve early 
      diagnosis. Their sensitivity is higher than that of conventional mycobacterial 
      culture in most paediatric studies.
