TI  - The use of the intubating laryngeal mask endotracheal tube with intubating 
      devices.
PG  - 249-50, table of contents
AB  - Despite adequate visualization of the vocal cords using specialized airway 
      devices, anatomical factors and the physical characteristics of the tube may 
      cause difficulty when performing endotracheal intubation. The endotracheal tube 
      designed for use with the intubating laryngeal mask airway may facilitate 
      intubation in these circumstances.
