TI  - Legionnaires' disease: a rare entity in Puerto Rico?
PG  - 251-3
AB  - Legionnaires' disease is a severe, often fatal pneumonia, caused by Legionella 
      pneumophila. Its incidence is reported about 6%. In Puerto Rico, there is no data 
      available of the prevalence of Legionnaires' disease. A case of Legionnaires' is 
      presented as well as data to support that the prevalence in our Island is higher 
      than the reported elsewhere.
