IP  - 8
DP  - 2001
TI  - [Diagnostic features of focal pulmonary tuberculosis in new cases].
PG  - 21-4
AB  - The authors examined 120 new cases of focal pulmonary tuberculosis (FPT) during 
      the good epidemic situation years (1982-1986) and 70 patients during the poor 
      epidemic situation years (1995-1999). The latter years were marked by a worse 
      social composition, more frequent contacts with those isolating bacteria, a more 
      severe course with weight loss, prolonged subfebrile temperatures, anemia, an 
      increasing tendency for lung tissue decay and even in large foci, a more frequent 
      bacterial isolation along with progressive immunodeficiency. New diagnostic 
      technologies, such as computed tomography, T-lymphocytic studies at the 
      subpopulational level by using monoclonal narrow-specific antibodies, adaptive 
      response tests that reflect the body's responsiveness, are of value in diagnosing 
      FPT.
