TI  - Laryngeal tuberculosis: an important diagnosis.
PG  - 878-80
AB  - The incidence of laryngeal tuberculosis is increasing worldwide. To ensure early 
      diagnosis it is important for physicians and otolaryngologists to recognize its 
      cardinal signs and symptoms. We present two recent cases of laryngeal 
      tuberculosis that presented to our department. We outline potential pitfalls in 
      diagnosis, and highlight the importance of obtaining a tissue diagnosis. The 
      literature is reviewed, and the treatment options outlined.
