DP  - 2000 Oct
TI  - Diffuse panbronchiolitis observed in a white man in Turkey.
PG  - 292-6
AB  - Diffuse panbronchiolitis (DPB) is a distinct clinicopathological entity which is 
      characterized by chronic recurrent sinopulmonary infection and inflammation. It 
      is prevalent in the Far East, but extremely rare in western countries. In this 
      report, we described the first Turkish case of DPB and also evaluated demographic 
      and diagnostic characteristics of 18 patients with DPB, previously reported from 
      non-Asian countries. We believe that DPB patients described from these countries 
      may also increase if this disease is taken into consideration in differential 
      diagnosis of sinopulmonary diseases. Another consideration is that, since the 
      treatment and prognosis of DPB are different from other obstructive pulmonary 
      diseases, it should not be mistaken for others.
