TI  - Augmented fiberoptic intubation.
PG  - 453-62
AB  - Patients who are difficult to intubate are randomly encountered. Patients who are 
      in the postoperative period or who have suffered trauma have a greater chance of 
      being difficult to intubate. The ability to quickly mobilize trained personnel 
      and advanced equipment provides the best chance for a good outcome for these 
      patients. Practice in placement of and intubation with LMAs is an important step 
      toward providing an extensive safety net for patients needing intubation.
