TI  - Dislodgement of bronchial foreign body during retrieval in children.
PG  - 333-5
AB  - Foreign body aspiration is a leading cause of death in children aged less than 1 
      year. The removal of a foreign body poses a great challenge to the skill of the 
      anaesthetist. Four cases are presented, analysing the part played by modes of 
      respiration in the dislodgement of a bronchial foreign body during its retrieval.
