TI  - Concomitant acute sinusitis and acute lung rejection.
PG  - 223-5
AB  - Two lung transplant recipients had concomitant acute sinusitis and acute lung 
      rejection. Antibiotics and decongestants alleviated the sinusitis, but the 
      symptoms of cough and dyspnea as well as spirometric defects necessitated 
      treatment of acute lung rejection. In patients with clinical evidence of acute 
      sinusitis after lung transplantation, concomitant acute lung rejection should be 
      suspected if dyspnea or pulmonary dysfunction is also present. This appears to be 
      the first report of concomitant acute sinusitis and acute lung rejection.
