TI  - Postpneumonectomy-like syndrome in an infant with right lung agenesis and left 
      main bronchus hypoplasia.
PG  - e43-5
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2009.02.023 [doi]
AB  - We report a 1-year-old child born with agenesis of the right lung who sustained 
      an episode of acute respiratory failure related to a postpneumonectomy-like 
      syndrome, with severe mediastinal shift and subsequent stretching and stenosis of 
      the left main bronchus. The insertion of an expandable prosthesis in the right 
      empty pleural space markedly improved the patient's clinical condition.
