TI  - Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor in the airway of a child.
PG  - 610-3
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2008.07.036 [doi]
AB  - This report describes a 9-year-old boy who was found to have an inflammatory 
      myofibroblastic tumor completely occluding the right mainstem bronchus. Initial 
      subtotal resection at an outside facility resulted in prompt recurrence of the 
      tumor. At our institution, total resection with bronchotomy and pericardial patch 
      repair resulted in an excellent outcome with no evidence of recurrence at 1 year 
      post-resection.
