VI  - 47
IP  - 19
DP  - 2008
TI  - A rare case of a tracheal fibroepithelial polyp treated by an endobronchial 
      resection.
PG  - 1723-6
AB  - This report describes a very rare case of a tracheal fibroepithelial polyp. A 
      69-year-old male had been treated in this department because of chronic 
      obstructive pulmonary disease since 2006. In July 2007, chest computed tomography 
      revealed a bronchial tumor located at the distal end of the trachea. A 
      bronchoscopic examination revealed a multilocular polyp. An endobronchial 
      resection was performed to remove the lesion. A tracheobronchial fibroepithelial 
      polyp is very rare. We herein describe and discuss the appropriate therapeutic 
      policy and also review the pertinent literature.
