VI  - 36 Suppl 1
DP  - 2008 Jul
TI  - The origins of the sniffing position and the Three Axes Alignment Theory for 
      direct laryngoscopy.
PG  - 23-7
AB  - The Three Axes Alignment Theory and the sniffing position for direct laryngoscopy 
      are the anatomical basis for direct laryngoscopy. This position has been one of 
      the hallmarks of airway management and yet its development is based on a small 
      number of descriptive texts published between 1852 and 1944. This paper explores 
      the origins of direct laryngoscopy and how the sniffing position came to be 
      described. The seemingly incongruent techniques of the rigid bronchoscopist and 
      direct laryngoscopist are discussed from an historical perspective.
