TI  - Diffuse alveolar hemorrhage: diagnosing it and finding the cause.
PG  - 258, 260, 264-5 passim
AB  - Diffuse alveolar hemorrhage is an acute, life-threatening event, and repeated 
      episodes can lead to organizing pneumonia, collagen deposition in small airways, 
      and, ultimately, fibrosis. Among the many conditions it can accompany are Wegener 
      granulomatosis, microscopic polyangiitis, Goodpasture syndrome, connective tissue 
      disorders, antiphospholipid antibody syndrome, infectious or toxic exposures, and 
      neoplastic conditions. Its many causes and presentations pose an important 
      challenge to the clinician.
