DP  - 2007
TI  - [Diagnosis and treatment of lung injuries].
PG  - 11-4
AB  - Overall 1218 patients with lung injuries were treated during 11 years. The rate 
      of deep wounds and injuries of central zone and root of lung was 24.9%. 
      Endoscopic and x-ray methods (especially computed tomography) were used for 
      diagnosis. Surgical tactics depended on type of injury. Resection of lung and 
      pneumonectomy were performed at 10.2% patients, closure of lung wound--at 41.3%. 
      Surgical treatment of lung wound with dissection and revision of wound canal was 
      performed at 42.6% patients with deep injuries. Classified surgical tactics 
      permits to reduce the rate of postoperative pulmonary complications from 62 to 
      11.6%, and lethality--from 11.2 to 3.1%.
