TI  - Carcinomatous lymphangitis as the initial manifestation of ovarian 
      adenocarcinoma.
PG  - 609-11
AB  - Carcinomatous lymphangitis accounts for approximately 8% of all cases of 
      metastatic pulmonary tumors. The most common primary sites are breast, lung, 
      stomach, prostate and pancreas. We describe herein the case of a 42-year-old 
      woman in whom the first manifestation of an ovarian adenocarcinoma was 
      carcinomatous lymphangitis of the lung, an unusual presentation of the disease.
