TI  - ACR Appropriateness Criteria on solitary pulmonary nodule.
PG  - 152-5
AB  - The solitary pulmonary nodule is traditionally defined as a relatively spherical 
      opacity 3 cm or less in diameter surrounded by lung parenchyma. The choice of 
      imaging test to evaluate solitary nodules is extensive. However, only 2 findings 
      are considered to be sufficient to preclude further evaluation: calcification in 
      a benign pattern and stability in size for more than 2 years.
