TI  - [Rigid bronchoscopy and foreign body. Obsolute procedure?].
PG  - 51-3
AB  - Foreign body aspiration represents an emergency event that usually requires 
      immediate medical intervention. In some cases this event may be misdiagnosed with 
      few, or absence of, clinical symptoms, but it can result in serious consequences. 
      The continuous technical improvements in minimally invasive procedures such as 
      bronchoscopy have permitted success in foreign body removal. We present a case of 
      aspiration of unusual foreign body (river stones) lodged in the left bronchial 
      tree, in a patient with epilepsy, and that were removed by rigid bronchoscopy.
