TI  - Case of pseudomembranous necrotizing tracheobronchial aspergillosis in an 
      immunocompetent host.
PG  - 279-82
AB  - A 44-year-old Korean male died of rapidly progressive respiratory failure and 
      refractory hypoxemia in 8 days after being admitted with a fever and dyspnea. The 
      patient was diagnosed with pseudomembranous necrotizing tracheobronchial 
      aspergillosis by fibroptic bronchoscopy and it was not related to an invasion of 
      the pulmonary parenchyma. To the best of our knowledge, this case represents a 
      patient with pseudomembranous necrotizing tracheobronchial aspergillosis that 
      developed in an immunocompetent host, rapidly resulting in airway obstruction 
      with acute respiratory failure and refractory hypoxemia without an invasion of 
      the pulmonary parenchyma.
