TI  - [Pulmonary Langerhans cell histiocytosis--case report].
PG  - 555-6
AB  - Pulmonary Langerhans cell histiocytosis is a rare interstitial lung disease. It's 
      morbidity is estimated at 4-5 person per million. The multiformity--from 
      benignity to severe--brings difficulties during the process of diagnosis. The 
      authors describe a case of 48-year-old woman with a benign pulmonary lung 
      histiocytosis. It is underlined the diagnostic quality of high resolution 
      tomography and bronchofibroscopy with bronchoalveolar lavage.
