TI  - Chondrodysplasia punctata: case report and review of audiological and ENT 
      features.
PG  - 233-6
AB  - Chondrodysplasia punctata is a term referring to a clinically heterogeneous group 
      of bone and cartilage dysplasias which cause characteristic epiphyseal stippling. 
      The condition can involve the ear, nose and throat in diverse ways at many 
      levels. We present a case of X-linked brachytelephalangic chondrodysplasia 
      punctata, which illustrates the features of this condition particularly relevant 
      to the audiological physician, otolaryngologist and neonatologist.
