TI  - [Middle lobe syndrome].
PG  - 279-81
AB  - Broncholithiasis is uncommon and usually a late complication of tuberculosis in 
      France. The most common cause of broncholithiasis is erosion by and extrusion of 
      a calcified lymph node into a bronchial lumen. Clinical symptoms are not specific 
      and diagnosis may be an endoscopic or a radiologic surprise. We report a case of 
      broncholithiasis in a patient with chronic cough. Fibroscopy established the 
      diagnosis by showing the broncholith.
