TI  - Diagnosis of pneumothorax on F-18 FDG PET after transbronchial biopsy.
PG  - 692-4
AB  - Transbronchial lung biopsy (TBLB) is associated with pneumothorax, 12% occurring 
      1 to 4 hours postprocedure (delayed pneumothorax). We report a case of a delayed 
      pneumothorax first diagnosed on a positron emission tomography (PET) scan 
      performed 5 days after TBLB. An early post-TBLB chest radiograph (after 1 hour) 
      had not demonstrated any pneumothorax. The delayed pneumothorax was later 
      confirmed with a repeat radiograph after the PET scan. Often, PET is performed to 
      diagnose or stage pulmonary lesions after TBLB rather than before. Therefore, 
      nuclear physicians must remain vigilant to recognize subtle pneumothoraces on PET 
      scans.
