TI  - Novel approach for a pulmonary bronchogenic cyst: a report of a case.
PG  - 249-51
AB  - We present a case of a bronchogenic pulmonary cyst in a 48-year-old patient. We 
      performed [corrected] mucoclasis using argon laser photocoagulation following 
      resection of mucosa, closure of some drainage bronchus, and covering of the inner 
      surface by the intrapulmonary bronchogenic cyst with an [corrected] absorbable 
      vicryl mesh. At [corrected] 4-year [corrected] follow-up, the patient had no 
      signs of recurrence.
