TI  - Unusual aero-digestive foreign bodies: tribulations and tragedies.
PG  - 1269-74
AB  - Aero-digestive foreign bodies are a common occurrence in infants and children. 
      The manifestations, hazards and consequences depend upon the location, nature of 
      the foreign body and the time lapse. This communication reports a series of four 
      cases with unusual course and consequences of aero-digestive foreign bodies. 
      These were generalized tetanus, hypernatremia and metabolic acidosis with 
      intra-cranial hemorrhage and severe pneumonia and empyema. Awareness of these 
      consequences would help treating doctors to take appropriate steps in devising 
      preventive and therapeutic strategies.
