TI  - Severe hemoptysis in a child after the Fontan procedure.
PG  - 515-8
AB  - There is an increased incidence of pulmonary hemorrhage and hemoptysis among 
      patients with congenital heart disease (CHD). The pathophysiology of pulmonary 
      hemorrhage in CHD includes pulmonary hypertension, pulmonary venous congestion, 
      aorto-pulmonary collaterals, pulmonary arteriovenous malformations, and dilated 
      bronchial arteries. We present the case of a 6-year old boy who required 
      treatment for massive hemoptysis after staged palliation for hypoplastic left 
      heart syndrome (HLHS). Effective management of this life threatening entity is 
      described as well as the anesthetic implications of performing rigid bronchoscopy 
      in a patient with the Fontan circulation and massive hemoptysis.
