TI  - Open surgical approach for a tooth aspirated during dental extraction: a case 
      report.
PG  - 49-50
AB  - Foreign body aspiration is a common problem in children necessitating prompt 
      recognition and early treatment to minimize the potentially serious and sometimes 
      even fatal consequences. Most foreign bodies can usually be extracted by skilful 
      application of endoscopic techniques. Nevertheless, spherical foreign bodies, 
      such as pen caps and some teeth remain difficult to manage. In this case report 
      clinical presentation and treatment options in the treatment of a patient who had 
      a tooth lodged in the right lung are discussed. The complications of foreign body 
      ingestion or aspiration associated with dental treatment is emphasized.
