VI  - 42
IP  - 2
DP  - 2005 Feb
TI  - Isolated unilateral pulmonary agenesis.
PG  - 170-2
AB  - Two cases of isolated pulmonary agenesis with no other associated congenital 
      abnormality are reported. First case was 13-year-old girl who presented for the 
      first time with chest infection and was found to have isolated unilateral 
      pulmonary agenesis and responded well to antibiotics, Second case was a 
      10-year-old girl who had presented with total duration of illness of one year 
      with clinical features suggestive of chronic chest infection with family history 
      of pulmonary tuberculosis and later found to have agenesis of upper lobe of left 
      lung in addition to having gastric aspirate positive for Mycobacterium 
      tuberculosis. She responded to anti tubercular therapy.
