TI  - Pseudo-tumor of the lung, a rare clinical presentation of dirofilariasis.
PG  - 109-10
AB  - INTRODUCTION: Pulmonary dirofilariasis is an uncommon entity. Known as a zoonotic 
      disease it can affect humans as a secondary host. A pseudo-tumor of the lung 
      called "coin" lesion is usually detected while performing a chest X-ray for 
      another reason. OBSERVATION: We present a case of pulmonary dirofilariasis due to 
      Dirofilaria sp. in a 72 year old immunocompetent patient who underwent surgery 
      for suspicion of a neoplasm. DISCUSSION: Human pulmonary dirofilariasis should be 
      evoked in asymptomatic patient from endemic area of canine dirofilariasis 
      presenting with a pseudo tumor of the lung.
