TI  - [Severe asthma complicated with large mucoid impaction: successful removal with 
      balloon catheter].
PG  - 914-8
AB  - A 28-year-old woman was hospitalized for renal transplantation. She suffered an 
      asthma attack after transplantation. Once this attack had ended after medical 
      treatment, she again experienced dyspnea after the 11th treatment day. A chest CT 
      showed mucoid impaction in the left main bronchus, atelectasis in the left lower 
      lobe, and pneumomediastinum. A huge mucoid impaction was removed with a balloon 
      catheter under mechanical ventilation without exacerbation of the mediastinal 
      emphysema. Mucoid impaction should be taken into account as a cause of dyspnea in 
      severe asthma if the maximum dose of beta-stimulant is not effective.
