TI  - Thoracic actinomycosis presented with tracheoesophageal fistula and fatal 
      pulmonary infection.
PG  - 1471-3
AB  - We report a case of a 60-year-old Saudi woman who developed tracheoesophageal 
      fistula and fatal pulmonary infection secondary to thoracic actinomycosis. The 
      cause, clinical presentation, radiological features and treatment of thoracic 
      actinomycosis are discussed.
