TI  - An interesting case of a wandering foreign body in the tracheobronchial tree.
PG  - 426-7
AB  - Inhaled foreign body (FB) is a rare clinical entity for the ENT surgeon. We 
      present a case of an inhaled foreign body in the right main bronchus shown to 
      move to the left main bronchus by repeat chest X-ray during a delay prior to 
      removal. The role of repeat chest X-ray if there is a significant delay before 
      removal of an inhaled foreign body and the optimal management are discussed.
