AB  - Expandable metallic stents have been used effectively to treat multiple 
      nonsurgical esophageal conditions. Here we describe two cases in 
      postpneumonectomy patients in which expandable esophageal stent placement 
      resulted in respiratory compromise requiring reintervention due to airway 
      compression.
