TI  - Isolated tracheal rupture caused by blunt trauma and the importance of early 
      diagnosis: a case report.
PG  - 217-9
AB  - Tracheal rupture usually occurs after blunt traumas. Isolated tracheal rupture is 
      an extremely rare condition. The diagnosis of isolated tracheal rupture is very 
      important for treatment and prognosis. Physical examination and imaging 
      techniques should be used to make the diagnosis. Lateral neck and chest X-rays 
      are very important for early diagnosis. Other techniques are thorax, neck 
      tomography and bronchoscopy. In this paper we present a case of isolated tracheal 
      rupture and discuss the early diagnostic techniques used.
