TI  - Bronchial sleeve resection for posttransplant stricture.
PG  - 2075-6
AB  - Nonanastomotic bronchial stenosis is a rare complication of lung transplantation. 
      We report a case of a bilateral lung transplant recipient who experienced 
      recalcitrant stenosis of the bronchus intermedius. All attempts at conservative 
      management failed, and the stricture was successfully treated by a 
      parenchymal-sparing segmental sleeve resection. Although rare, this is an 
      important technique in the management of this difficult problem.
