AB  - Fibre-optic bronchoscopy has traditionally been performed by respiratory 
      physicians and registrars. It is an invaluable investigation for diagnosing lung 
      cancer and other respiratory diseases. Modern bronchoscopy techniques make the 
      procedure safe for most patients, apart from those who are gravely ill, or who 
      have a gross reduction in respiratory reserve (Stradling, 1991).
