TI  - Management of a large bronchial haemangioma in an infant.
PG  - 429-33
AB  - Haemangiomas are the most common soft tissue tumor of infancy. Despite the benign 
      and trivial nature of most cutaneous haemangiomas, airway haemangiomas are rare 
      but potentially life threatening. We report the case of a 9-week-old infant with 
      a left main stem bronchial haemangioma. This was successfully treated with the 
      oral corticosteroids. We discuss the current available treatments for 
      haemangiomas and highlight that treatment should be specific to each individual 
      case.
