TI  - Metastatic intracranial abscesses of bronchopulmonary origin.
PG  - 277-80
AB  - Intracranialabscesses are serious, life-threatening infections despite recent 
      advances in diagnosis and treatment. We report the case of a child with 
      metastatic brain abscesses and a chronic, sharp foreign body of the bronchus. Its 
      presentation and endoscopic appearance and the microbiology of the abscesses are 
      detailed. The detection of bacteria of respiratory origin should lead to a search 
      for a bronchopulmonary source of contamination.
