TI  - New procedure: bronchoscopic endobronchial sealing; a new mode of managing 
      hemoptysis.
PG  - 2066-9
AB  - Six patients with hemoptysis were treated by endobronchial sealing, with n-butyl 
      cyanoacrylate, of the bleeding segment or subsegment. There was an immediate 
      arrest of bleeding without any recurrence for a mean follow-up period of 127 (+/- 
      67.17) days. Endobronchial sealing appears to be an effective method of managing 
      hemoptysis.
