TI  - [Nursing of intubation].
PG  - 458-62
AB  - Recent developments in noninvasive ventilation allow the intensivists to delay 
      the time o intubation of the patient admitted to the ICU. This new possibility of 
      a gain in time leads to the fact that those patients who are intubated in the 
      ICLI, are patients with a very compromised hemodynamic and respiratory situation. 
      For this reason, we developed a specific protocol regarding the intubation 
      procedure of this kind of patients. This paper reviews our strategies for 
      endotracheal tube positioning in critically ill patients and shows the 
      fundamental role of the nurses during this procedure.
