TI  - [Surgical treatment of bronchogenic and enterogenic mediastinal cysts complicated 
      by intrathoracic compression of respiratory tracts in children].
PG  - 26-8
AB  - In the clinic there were operated on 8 patients with bronchogenic and enterogenic 
      mediastinal cyst, complicated by intrathoracic compression of respiratory ways. 
      In 2 children postoperative complications occurred. In presence of secondary 
      tracheomalacia, caused by tracheal compression by bronchogenic cyst, aortopexy 
      was done in conjunction with the cystic formation excision. All the patients 
      survived. In 6 children satisfactory result was noted, in 2--relatively 
      satisfactory one.
