VI  - 22
IP  - 2
DP  - 2001 Jun
TI  - Bronchoscopy. Year 2001 and beyond.
PG  - 225-39, vii
AB  - The current revolution in technology, imaging, and information processing will be 
      of major influence on bronchoscopy within the next two decades. Clinicians will 
      be able to visualize structures in vivo that up to now only the pathologist could 
      see. Clinicians will reach anatomic structures that are inaccessible by the 
      bronchoscope, yet treat diseases that are still the domain of surgeons, medical 
      oncologists, and radiotherapists. Clinicians will be able to communicate online 
      worldwide, improving standards of patient care, teaching, and finally even 
      perform interventional procedures by way of networks. Because of the exponential 
      growth of sciences like nanotechnology and biotechnology, these changes will come 
      very rapidly. The new quality of these intelligent instruments will demand a new 
      ideological and ethical discourse on the future of science in general.
