TI  - Bronchoscopically-guided conformal radiation therapy for radiographically occult 
      lung carcinoma.
PG  - 269-71
AB  - Radiographically occult lung carcinoma has a very good prognosis after complete 
      surgical resection. In medically inoperable patients three-dimensional conformal 
      radiation therapy cannot be performed, as computed tomography scan images fail to 
      localize the disease. Presented here is an original technique of marking 
      radiographically occult tumors by fiberoptic bronchoscopy, applied on four 
      patients. No short-term complications were recorded. All the patients are alive, 
      with no evidence of disease, after a mean follow-up of 15 months.
