TI  - A rare case of bronchial glomus tumor.
PG  - 95-8
AB  - A 48-year-old man was admitted because of bloody sputum in whom a chest computed 
      tomography (CT) scan and fiberoptic bronchoscopy demonstrated a polypoid tumor in 
      the left main bronchus. The tumor was surgically resected, and the pathological 
      and immunohistochemical findings led to diagnosis of the tumor as a bronchial 
      glomus tumor.
