AB  - Inhalation of sharp bones by infants is an uncommon but hazardous occurrence. 
      management relies not only on a high index of clinical suspicion and timely 
      treatment but also demands expertise in therapeutic bronchoscopy. The potential 
      complications and the management of this condition are reviewed.
