TI  - Pseudomembranous aspergillus bronchitis in a double-lung transplanted patient: 
      unusual radiographic and CT features.
PG  - 1547-9
AB  - Pseudomembranous aspergillus bronchitis is considered as an early form of 
      invasive pulmonary aspergillosis, a well-known airway infection in 
      immunocompromised patients. Radiologic features concerning invasive aspergillosis 
      of the airways have been reported. However, we describe here an unusual feature 
      of invasive aspergillus bronchitis, never reported to date, observed in a 
      double-lung transplanted patient. Chest radiograph and CT revealed significant 
      peribronchial thickening without any parenchymal involvement.
