TI  - Recurrent respiratory papillomatosis.
PG  - 35-7
AB  - Recurrent respiratory papillomatosis is characterized by the appearance of benign 
      laryngeal squamous papillomas in childhood. Lung involvement is rare. We report a 
      case of childhood laryngeal papillomas who developed tracheobronchial papillomas 
      and a nodule in the lung after a period of 21 years. Frequent sampling of 
      pulmonary lesions to detect malignant transformation is suggested as prognosis of 
      lung lesions are worse in comparison to laryngeal papillomas.
