TI  - Right tracheal bronchus in an infant with congenital diaphragmatic hernia.
PG  - 621-3
LID - 10.1055/s-0029-1220779 [doi]
AB  - Neonates with congenital diaphragmatic hernia (CDH) often have other major 
      malformations. Anatomic airway anomalies associated with CDH include congenital 
      stenosis, pulmonary hypoplasia, and abnormal bronchial branching. We describe an 
      infant with CDH who, after developing recurrent upper-lobe atelectasis, was found 
      to have a right tracheal bronchus. This clinically significant anomaly can have 
      important and potentially preventable adverse consequences.
