TI  - Bacterial tracheitis--not always primary.
PG  - 409-11
AB  - A child presented with features of bacterial tracheitis with complete response to 
      therapy. He presented with a recurrence one week later. A foreign body in the 
      tracheal wall was diagnosed and removed by bronchoscopy. Tracheal intubation for 
      airway management and tracheal toileting are not enough in bacterial tracheitis; 
      bronchoscopy should be considered to diagnose any underlying cause.
