TI  - Mucoid impaction after segmental resection of lung.
PG  - 249-51
AB  - Lung segmentectomy is generally considered as a standard procedure in general 
      thoracic surgery. Anatomical variations of pulmonary segmentation may, however, 
      make it difficult to determine the precise area of resection during 
      segmentectomy. Incomplete pulmonary sub-lobar resection may produce unusual 
      radiographic features. Herein, we report a case of bronchial atresia after lung 
      segmentectomy.
