TI  - [Bronchial schwannoma diagnosis by surgical treatment; report of a case].
PG  - 903-6
AB  - 18-year-old male was referred to our hospital due to persistent cough. The 
      patient was admitted for the investigation of the abnormal shadow on a chest 
      X-ray and chest computed tomography (CT). Chest CT showed a 2.5 cm nodular shadow 
      in the right lower lobe. Bronchofiberscopy revealed the polypoid lesion at the 
      right lower lobe bronchus obstructing the entire lumen of B8-10. The tumor 
      surface was smooth and rich in small vessels. Right lower lobectomy was peformed. 
      The diagnosis of schwannoma was confirmd with the S-100 positive 
      immunohistochemical stain. Bronchial schwannoma is relatively rare disease; less 
      than 90 cases have been reported with respect to schwannoma of case report in 
      Japan.
