TI  - Advances in respiratory imaging.
PG  - 879-900, vi
AB  - Although conventional radiography is still the first diagnostic imaging approach 
      to respiratory disease, CT is proving to be invaluable as an adjunctive procedure 
      in characterizing nasal and thoracic pathologic findings. CT eliminates 
      superimposition of overlying structures and offers superior contrast resolution 
      as compared with conventional radiography. These advantages allow for more 
      precise characterization and localization of lesions and are invaluable for 
      guiding rhinoscopic, bronchoscopic, and surgical procedures.
