TI  - Lymphoepithelioma-like carcinoma in the trachea: report of a case.
PG  - 584-6
AB  - Lymphoepithelioma-like carcinoma (LELC) is a non-nasopharyngeal undifferentiated 
      carcinoma with prominent lymphoid infiltration. To our knowledge, only two cases 
      of LELC in the trachea have ever been reported. This tumor has a strong 
      association with the Epstein-Barr virus (EBV), which is especially prevalent in 
      Asians and absent in Caucasians. We report a case of tracheal LELC with 
      EBV-association in a 22-year-old man. The patient was treated with tracheal 
      resection and anastomosis, followed later by adjuvant radiotherapy.
