TI  - H-type tracheoesophageal fistula with type III laryngotracheoesophageal cleft.
PG  - 1373-6
AB  - H-type tracheoesophageal fistula and laryngotracheoesophageal cleft are both rare 
      anomalies. Laryngotracheoesophageal clefts are identified as a part of 
      Opitz-Frias syndrome. We report a neonate with this combination of rare 
      congenital anomalies. These associated malformations can have major implications 
      in terms of resuscitation, diagnosis and surgical management, which are 
      discussed.
