DP  - 2006 Jul-Sep
TI  - An experience of 42 cases of bronchoscopy at Saidu Group of Teaching Hospitals, 
      Swat.
PG  - 59-62
AB  - BACKGROUND: The objectives of our study were to find out the frequency in terms 
      of age and sex of the patients, type and site of foreign bodies, clinical 
      manifestations and management with rigid ventilating bronchoscope. METHODS: It 
      was a descriptive study carried out in the department of otolaryngology and head 
      and neck surgery at Saidu Teaching Hospital swat, and was conducted from March 
      2005 to March 2006. A total of 42 cases collected from March 2005 to March 2006, 
      admitted through casualty, OPD and referred by pediatric unit. All of them 
      subjected to bronchoscopy as an emergency as well as an elective procedure. 
      RESULTS: A total of 42 cases were included in the study. In 37 cases (88.09%) 
      foreign bodies were removed successfully, while 4 cases (9.52%) were having no 
      foreign body, only mucous plug was removed. One patient (2.32%) died due to 
      cardiac arrest.
