TI  - Postpneumonectomy syndrome: a spectrum of clinical presentations.
PG  - 1185-8
AB  - Postpneumonectomy syndrome has classically been described as a late complication 
      after pneumonectomy where gradually increasing shortness of breath develops 
      secondary to mediastinal shift. We present our experience and a review of the 
      literature demonstrating a variety of clinical scenarios that, when necessary, 
      were successfully managed with mediastinal repositioning.
