TI  - The dispersed neuroendocrine system, its bronchopulmonary elements, and 
      neuroendocrine tumors presumed to be derived from them: myths, mistaken notions, 
      and misunderstandings.
PG  - 178-82
AB  - The increasing recognition of the dispersed neuroendocrine system and its 
      importance in human physiology has impacted our understanding of physiology, 
      pathophysiology, and histopathology. It has been the subject of a great deal of 
      controversy and debate, giving rise to certain misunderstandings. This article 
      attempts to put some of these issues in perspective, especially as they relate to 
      the bronchopulmonary tree.
