TI  - Treatment of a benign tracheoesophageal fistula in a ventilator dependent 
      quadriplegic patient.
PG  - 554-5
AB  - Management of an acquired benign tracheoesophageal fistula in a patient who is 
      dependent on mechanical ventilation is controversial, since the usual procedure 
      is weaning before repair. Here, we describe surgical treatment of a 
      tracheoesophageal fistula in a quadriplegic patient with 28 months of follow-up, 
      who has to remain permanently on mechanical ventilation with a tracheostomy 
      cannula.
