TI  - Stridor in Crohn disease and the use of infliximab.
PG  - 579-81
AB  - Extraintestinal manifestations of Crohn disease are well recognized. Upper airway 
      obstruction is a very rare but important complication that usually responds to 
      high-dose steroids. We report a case of Crohn disease initially presenting with 
      respiratory symptoms and subsequently resulting in acute severe upper airway 
      obstruction, which failed to respond to steroids but dramatically responded to 
      the first documented use of infliximab in this context.
