TI  - [Current endoscopic treatments for cicatricial stenoses of the trachea].
PG  - 11-7
AB  - Endoscopic techniques in the treatment of patients with cicatricial stenoses of 
      the trachea have become customary in clinical practice. They may be used alone 
      and in combination with open surgery. The present paper discusses various 
      endoscopic therapy modalities. The long-term results of stenting of the trachea 
      for its stenosis are recent and of practical importance, which permits revision 
      of the established opinion on this treatment option.
