TI  - Deep tracheal laceration after balloon dilation for benign tracheobronchial 
      stenosis: case reports of two patients.
PG  - 529-35
AB  - We report two cases of deep tracheal laceration in female patients after balloon 
      dilation for benign tracheobronchial stenosis. Immediate post-procedure 
      bronchoscopy and CT including 3D reconstructions showed deep lacerations in the 
      posterior tracheal wall. Clinically, the patients' dyspnoea subsided and there 
      has been no recurrence during follow-up after balloon dilation. On the follow-up 
      3D-reconstructed CT scans obtained 2 months and 8 months following balloon 
      dilation, respectively, the lacerations had healed completely and there was 
      considerable improvement in lumen size.
