TI  - Fractured tracheostomy tube in the tracheo-bronchial tree.
PG  - 303-4
AB  - Tracheostomy is a life saving procedure and many a times patients are discharged 
      with permanent tracheostomy tubes. However, fracture of tracheostomy tube with 
      subsequent migration into the tracheobronchial tree is uncommon and carries the 
      potentially fatal risk of respiratory obstruction. In this report, a case of a 
      6-year-old boy is presented, who had aspirated a fractured tracheostomy tube 
      which had lodged in the left bronchus.
