TI  - An unusual cause of chronic cough. Foreign body aspiration.
PG  - C1-3
AB  - Foreign body aspiration (FBA) is a serious medical problem, causing thousands of 
      deaths nationally each year. Clinical presentations range from acute suffocation 
      and death to chronic and subtle respiratory symptoms. Although FBA is more common 
      in children, adult patients are also at risk. We present a classic case of FBA in 
      an adult male with a history of alcohol abuse and chronic cough.
