TI  - Recurrence and malignant transformation in solitary fibrous tumour of the pleura.
PG  - 65-7
AB  - Solitary fibrous tumours of the pleura are mesenchymal neoplasms and recurrence 
      with malignant progression after complete resection rarely occurs. In the case of 
      a 76-year-old patient we found multifocal recurrence with malignant 
      transformation within six months following primary excision. Even though the vast 
      majority of these tumours are benign, complete resection as well as clinical and 
      radiological follow-up are highly recommended because of the potentially adverse 
      biological behaviour and the lack of radical treatment options other than 
      surgery.
