TI  - Primary pulmonary nodular amyloidosis.
PG  - 173-5
AB  - Primary nodular amyloidosis of the lung is an uncommon manifestation. The disease 
      runs a benign course, but offers diagnostic problems due to non-specific 
      radiological features entering the big field of the solitary nodule. We describe 
      the case of a 60 year old man with multiple nodules on the left lung operated on 
      diagnostic and therapeutic video-assisted thoracoscopy and discuss the 
      possibilities, if any, of suspecting such a disease through radiologic 
      characteristics along with findings from the patient's history, physical 
      examination and laboratory tests.
