TI  - Bronchiolitis obliterans organising pneumonia: a treatable condition.
PG  - 222-5
AB  - Bronchiolitis obliterans organising peumonia BOO) is an uncommon inflammatory 
      lung condition involving the terminal bronchioles and alveoli, which is 
      responsive to treatment with corticosteroids. Patients usually present with 
      dyspnoea, cough and fever. Two cases are described here; both had haemoptysis and 
      were initially treated as community acquired pneumonia. Diagnosis was made on 
      lung biopsy and there was rapid resolution after a course of prednisolone.
