TI  - Computed tomography diagnosis of tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica.
PG  - 319-21
AB  - Tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica (TO) is a rare benign disease 
      characterized by the presence of osseous and cartilaginous submucosal nodules 
      projecting into the tracheobronchial tree. Most cases are asymptomatic and 
      discovered incidentally at post-mortem. We identified a case of TO on thoracic 
      spiral CT and confirmed the diagnosis of bronchoscopy. This article reviews the 
      imaging characteristics of TO, and shows the 3-D virtual bronchoscopic and 
      multiplanar reconstruction appearances of TO.
