VI  - 79
IP  - 5
DP  - 2005 May
TI  - Therapeutic management of broncholithiasis.
PG  - 1774-6
AB  - Broncholithiasis is characterized by calcified perihilar and mediastinal lymph 
      nodes eroding into the tracheobronchial tree. We report herein 4 cases of 
      symptomatic broncholithiasis managed by surgical resection in 2 cases and 
      bronchoscopic removal in 2 cases. From our experience and from the literature 
      review, bronchoscopic removal should be considered in cases of uncomplicated and 
      loose broncholithiasis, whereas surgical management should be chosen first in 
      complicated cases such as obstructive pneumonitis, bronchiectasis, massive 
      hemoptysis, and bronchoesophageal fistulas.
