TI  - Successful late restoration of traumatic distal bronchial separation.
PG  - 195-7
AB  - Traumatic distal bronchial interruption is unusual. A 42-year-old male with 
      history of blunt injury to his chest and abdomen 20 years previously presented 
      with recurrent pneumonia of the right lung. Patient's middle and lower lobes were 
      partially atelectatic and the right intermediate bronchus was found completely 
      dehisced at the time of surgical exploration. A direct re-implantation of 
      intermediate bronchus was successfully performed. At late follow-up the 
      anastomosis had healed well without any stricture and patient remains without 
      symptoms.
