TI  - Congenital nasal pyriform aperture stenosis with semilobar holoprosencephaly.
PG  - 93-6
AB  - We describe a child who has congenital nasal pyriform aperture stenosis with 
      single maxillary central incisor, holoprosencephaly and central diabetes 
      insipidus without any apparent anterior pituitary dysfunction. Conservative 
      management of the congenital nasal pyriform aperture stenosis is adopted and 
      management of diabetes insipidus is described. A literature review is undertaken.
