TI  - Percutaneous dilatation tracheostomy: which technique is the best for the 
      critically ill patient, and how can we gather further scientific evidence?
PG  - 319-21
AB  - Percutaneous dilatation tracheostomy in the intensive care setting presents an 
      increasingly important concept for establishing a large-bore tracheal airway with 
      minimal surgical intervention. Over the last years, different technical solutions 
      have been studied to assess their respective risks and benefits to determine 
      whether one method is actually superior. A recent observational study comparing 
      two such techniques prompted this commentary, which reviews the current 
      literature, comments on study design and suggests interesting topics for future 
      research in this field.
