PMID- 15458619
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20041130
LR  - 20091103
IS  - 0300-2896 (Print)
IS  - 0300-2896 (Linking)
VI  - 40
IP  - 9
DP  - 2004 Sep
TI  - [Localized fibrous tumors of the pleura: clinical and surgical evaluation].
PG  - 419-21
AB  - Solitary fibrous tumors of the pleura are uncommon and mainly arise in the pleura 
      itself. Such tumors are generally asymptomatic and slow-growing. We report a 
      series of 10 cases (8 men and 2 women with a mean age of 58.6 years) treated over 
      a period of 54 months. The tumors were classified histologically as benign or 
      malignant according to the criteria used by England. The treatment of choice was 
      complete resection of the tumor. Six posterolateral thoracotomies and 4 
      video-assisted resections were performed. Histology showed a mixture of 
      fibroblast-like cells and collagenous stroma. Sarcomatous degeneration was 
      observed in the excised tumor of 1 patient. The patients were followed for a mean 
      of 23.9 months. We conclude that although fibrous tumors of the pleura are 
      considered benign histologically, complete resection and follow up for all 
      patients are recommended.
