TI  - Successful management of concommitant blunt injury to the trachea, esophagus, and 
      cervical spine in a 6-year-old girl.
PG  - 1130-2
AB  - A 6-year-old girl sustained an unusual constellation of injuries after blunt 
      trauma sustained in a motor vehicle accident. Transection of the trachea and 
      esophagus were managed successfully by repair through a median sternotomy while 
      the patient was on cardiopulmonary bypass. A cervical spinal injury was fixated 
      with halo traction and a femur fracture with internal fixation.
