TI  - [Foreign bodies in the lower respiratory tract--experience based on material 
      gathered in the ENT Department of Kalisz between 1984-2001].
PG  - 503-7
AB  - Between 1984 and 2001, 33 patients were treated because of foreign bodies in 
      their lower respiratory tract. The age of patients ranged from 0 to 74 years, but 
      the most numerous group was children between 0 and 5 years--16 cases and between 
      6 and 15 years--9 cases. The most often met foreign bodies were: organic--17 
      cases, metal bodies 7, plastic 7. We found proliferous changes in 2 patients. In 
      all cases foreign bodies were removed by means of rigid bronchoscopy. In 30 cases 
      they were treated within 48 hours. Only in one case, a ring, retained for 6 
      weeks. We didn't have any complications.
