TI  - The evolution of lung cancer screening.
PG  - 234-8
AB  - In the 1970s, four trials failed to demonstrate any mortality reduction using a 
      combination of chest X-ray (CXR) and/or sputum cytology. The recent early lung 
      cancer action project (ELCAP) demonstrated that modern screening is capable of 
      detecting Stage I lung cancers. Bronchial epithelial changes leading up to 
      cancers are now being understood to include histologic changes and genetic 
      alterations. Emerging molecular markers detected in sputum and serum show promise 
      in the future of lung cancer screening.
