TI  - Delayed diagnosis of laryngeal foreign body.
PG  - 143-4
AB  - Aspiration of a foreign body is a recognized cause of accidental death in 
      children. Paediatricians are aware of the symptoms of inhaled foreign bodies in 
      the lower respiratory tract. However, symptoms which suggest impaction in the 
      larynx do not appear to raise the same index of suspicion of a foreign body. One 
      case of laryngeal foreign body is described with a delay in diagnosis of five 
      days. The clinical presentation, investigations and management are discussed.
