DP  - 2002
TI  - [Clinical presentation and course of sarcoidosis under the conditions of the West 
      Urals].
PG  - 37-40
AB  - The specific features of the clinical presentation and course of respiratory 
      sarcoidosis (S) and the efficiency of its treatment were studied in 109 new cases 
      in the Perm Region. The incidence of S is higher among residents from towns with 
      developed heavy industry, mainly in females. Primary chronic S was predominant 
      (89.9%). The efficiency of treatment in the patients was 69.5%. The results of 
      treatment were worse in the untimely detection of S. The recovery rates were 
      higher with corticosteroid tablets used continuously (87.5%) and those were lower 
      with their intermittent use (82.9%).
