TI  - Broncholithiasis and lithoptysis associated with silicosis.
PG  - 1057-9
AB  - A case of broncholithiasis associated with massive silicosis is reported, showing 
      a rare aspect of parenchymal lesions generating broncholiths as well as the 
      presence of recurrent lithoptysis, with subsequent regression of radiological 
      lesions. Aetiological, clinical, physiopathological, and radiological aspects of 
      the disease are discussed, demonstrating the importance of the use of computed 
      tomography in diagnosis. The mineralogical analysis of expectorated fragments is 
      also shown.
