TI  - Subcutaneous emphysema and pneumomediastinum as presenting manifestations of 
      neonatal tracheal injury.
PG  - 499-501
AB  - Neonatal tracheal injury/perforation is an uncommon complication of traumatic 
      deliveries or endotracheal intubation. We present a case of neonatal tracheal 
      injury following delivery at term that presented with subcutaneous emphysema and 
      pneumomediastinum before any attempt at intubation. The clinical course, 
      treatment, and outcome are described.
