DP  - 2001
TI  - Broncho-gastric fistula complicating transthoracic esophagectomy.
PG  - 271-3
AB  - Tracheo-esophageal and broncho-esophageal fistulas are recognized complications 
      in advanced esophageal cancers. The common complications seen after transthoracic 
      esophagectomy include pulmonary complications, anastomotic leaks, gastric stasis, 
      and anastomotic strictures. A broncho-gastric fistula is a very rare complication 
      of transthoracic esophagectomy and has been reported anecdotally in the 
      literature. We report a patient who underwent a transthoracic esophagectomy and 
      developed a broncho-gastric fistula caused by a staple from the stomach tube 
      suture line eroding into the right bronchus. Diagnosis was made by fiberoptic 
      bronchoscopy. The patient was successfully treated with re-exploratory 
      thoracotomy and closure of the fistula.
