TI  - Anesthetic management of acquired tracheoesophageal fistula: a brief report.
PG  - 903-5, table of contents
AB  - Tracheoesophageal fistula may be either a congenital lesion or an acquired 
      condition, most often resulting from foreign body ingestion. Location of the 
      lesion has implications for anesthetic management and single lung ventilation may 
      be required to facilitate surgical repair. In pediatric patients, intentional 
      mainstem intubation may be required.
