TI  - Intramural neurofibroma of the trachea treated by multiple stents.
PG  - 583-4
AB  - The case history is presented of a patient in whom an intramural tracheal 
      neurofibroma developed, causing severe airway stenosis. The patient was treated 
      with multiple stents over a period of 5 years because of progression of the 
      disease and associated airflow limitation. Clinicians should be aware of this 
      rare complication of neurofibromatosis.
