TI  - Successful treatment of intratracheal cuterebrosis in two cats.
PG  - 304-8
AB  - Two cases of feline intratracheal myiasis due to Cuterebra spp. larvae are 
      reported. Both cats presented with inspiratory dyspnea and a nonproductive cough. 
      One larva was successfully removed during thoracotomy, and the other was removed 
      during bronchoscopy using forceps passed through a bronchoscope operating 
      channel. Clinical signs were alleviated following removal of the larvae.
