TI  - Aortobronchial fistula after aortic dissection type B.
PG  - 259-62
AB  - Although rare, aortobronchial fistula complicates thoracic aortic surgery. 
      Correct diagnosis and the infectious nature of the lesion are the most important 
      conditions to define, for the following best therapy. We presented a case of 
      non-infectious postsurgical aortobronchial fistula, revealed by 
      computed-tomographic scan and angiography procedure, treated with prosthetic 
      graft replacement and broad spectrum antibiotic therapy. In the case of infection 
      our policy is homograft replacement. Computed tomography, being able to make 
      diagnosis, should be performed as the initial technique.
