TI  - Progressive esophageal leiomyomatosis with respiratory compromise.
PG  - 247-50
AB  - Leiomyomatosis is a rare neoplastic condition of the pediatric esophagus. 
      Presenting symptoms usually overlap with more common esophageal disorders, 
      namely, gastroesophageal reflux. A patient is presented in whom leiomyomatosis 
      progressed to the point of causing cachexia and respiratory compromise.
