IS  - 0047-1852 (Linking)
VI  - 67
IP  - 5
DP  - 2009 May
TI  - [Racemose hemangioma of the bronchial artery].
PG  - 1038-41
AB  - Racemose hemangioma of the bronchial arteries is a rare abnormality and is 
      characterized by enlarged and convoluted bronchial arteries arranged segmentally 
      along the longitudinal axis of bronchus. Primary racemose hemangioma may arise 
      from inborn malformation, and secondary one may develop following primary 
      inflammatory, stenosing or deforming diseases of the bronchus, the peribronchial 
      tissues and the surrounding lung tissues. The symptom at onset is usually 
      hemoptysis. Although the typical treatments have not been established, various 
      treatments, like embolization or ligation of the bronchial arteries and surgical 
      resection of the involved area of lung, were reported. However the term 'Racemose 
      hemangioma' seems to be used only in Japan, so it is favorable to make a 
      consensus of its definition among countries.
