TI  - A neurologic etiology for tracheomalacia?
PG  - 885-7
LID - 10.1016/j.ijporl.2009.02.008 [doi]
AB  - To date, major works on tracheomalacia have assumed a structural etiology and 
      have proposed therapies as such. We describe a possible neurologic etiology for 
      tracheomalacia in a child with clinically significant tracheomalacia that 
      resolved in synchrony with each treatment of his recurring hydrocephalus. 
      Endoscopy confirms remarkable expansion of tracheal diameter 7 days after 
      decreasing intracranial pressure. The possibility of a neurologic etiology for 
      tracheomalacia casts this condition in a new light with potential therapeutic 
      implications.
