TI  - Elevated FDG uptake in right middle segmental bronchus impacted with foreign 
      body.
PG  - 241-2
LID - 10.1097/RLU.0b013e31819a2037 [doi]
AB  - A 62-year-old man with recurrent episodes of coughing underwent a whole-body FDG 
      PET/CT scan to evaluate possible lung malignancy. The PET images showed increased 
      FDG uptake in the right side of the bronchus corresponding to a foreign body on 
      the concurrent CT images. The foreign body was subsequently removed through 
      bronchofiberscopy and was proven to be a fishbone.
