DP  - 2008 Oct
TI  - Primary tracheobronchial amyloidosis.
PG  - 881-4
LID - S1806-37132008001000015 [pii]
AB  - Tracheobronchial amyloidosis is an uncommon localized form of amyloidosis, 
      characterized by amyloid deposits restricted to the trachea, main bronchi and 
      segmental bronchi. We present the case of a retired 67-year-old man with 
      long-term progressive dyspnea, wheezing and chest pain. A diagnosis of 
      tracheobronchial amyloidosis was made after the third fiberoptic bronchoscopy and 
      histological confirmation through Congo red staining of tissue samples.
