TI  - Combined endoscopic approach in the treatment of benign broncho-oesophageal 
      fistula.
PG  - 1024-5
LID - 10.1136/thx.2007.091686 [doi]
AB  - The treatment of benign broncho-oesophageal fistula is usually surgical but 
      sometimes other methods of treatment are preferred. The case history is described 
      of an adult in poor general condition in which an endoscopic approach combined 
      with the use of fibrin glue on the bronchial side and metallic clips on the 
      oesophageal side was used to close the fistula.
