TI  - Coccidioides immitis: two cases of misidentified mycosis.
PG  - 377-9
AB  - In the present report, two cases of pulmonary coccidioidomycosis that caused a 
      diagnostic confusion are presented. The first case was initially misdiagnosed as 
      nonsmall cell carcinoma, and both cases were initially misidentified as 
      blastomycosis because of the presence of an atypical morphological form of 
      Coccidioides immitis.
