DP  - 2008 Sep
TI  - [Niemann-Pick disease type B identified following an episode of 
      bronchopneumonia].
PG  - 861-6
AB  - Niemann Pick disease type B (NPD type B) is a rare autosomal recessive lipid 
      storage disorder, characterized by a partial deficiency of sphingomyelinase. We 
      report the case of an adult male patient affected by NPD type B and diagnosed at 
      39-years-of age. Pulmonary CT scan revealed a cranio-caudal gradient with nodular 
      centrilobular ground glass opacities and thickening of the interlobular septa. 
      Pathological examination of the bronchoalveolar lavage showed foamy alveolar 
      macrophages and vacuolated bronchial epithelial cells on bronchial biopsy. 
      Diagnostic confirmation was achieved by a decrease in cell lysosomal enzyme 
      activity and by the presence of the homozygous DeltaR608 mutation in the acid 
      sphingomyelinase gene (SMPD1).
