TI  - [Tracheomalacia inadvertently diagnosed by CT angiography originally performed to 
      rule out pulmonary embolism].
PG  - 666-7, 752
AB  - Tracheomalacia is a frequent disease in the older population involving excessive 
      airway collapse and it may present symptoms similar to pulmonary emboli. This is 
      a case study depicting a patient's inadvertent breathing during a CT scan, 
      performed to rule out pulmonary emboli. This examination revealed significant 
      tracheomalacia, a condition usually diagnosed by bronchoscopy or specially 
      tailored CT.
