TI  - Simultaneous cytological diagnosis of herpes simplex virus infection and primary 
      lung cancer: report of two cases.
PG  - 818-22
LID - 10.1002/dc.20921 [doi]
AB  - Herpes simplex is an uncommon cause of lower respiratory tract infection that 
      requires prompt diagnosis and treatment to prevent late complications. We report 
      two cases with simultaneous herpes simplex virus infection of the lower 
      respiratory tract and lung carcinoma. Cytology of bronchial brushing and washing 
      fluids and postbronchoscopic sputum established the diagnosis, which was further 
      corroborated by real-time polymerase chain reaction.
