TI  - Medical ablation of endobronchial mucormycosis with Amphotericin-B.
PG  - 861-5
AB  - A 56 years male diabetic patient presented with recurrent left upper lobe 
      pneumonia. Fiberoptic bronchoscopy revealed extraluminal compression of left main 
      bronchus with an endobronchial mass obstructing the left upper lobe orifice. The 
      lesion resembled bronchial adenoma. However histological examination revealed 
      mucormycosis. Timely diagnosis followed by medical intervention with intravenous 
      Amphotericin B, coupled with proper management of diabetes, ablated the tumor. 
      Relevant literature on the subject is reviewed.
