TI  - Diagnostic work-up of pleural effusions.
PG  - 4-13
LID - 10.1159/000112221 [doi]
AB  - A wide range of diseases may be the cause of an accumulation of fluid in the 
      pleural space. Pleural effusion is a major diagnostic problem, since the pleura 
      is an inner cavity with no direct access. The aim of this review is to provide a 
      practical approach to the investigation of the patient presenting with pleural 
      effusion. This should help to accurately diagnose pleural effusion and keep 
      time-consuming, but necessary, invasive investigations to the minimum.
