VI  - 48
IP  - 12
DP  - 2007 Dec
TI  - [Differential diagnoses of dyspnoea].
PG  - 1389-99; quiz 1400
AB  - Dyspnoea is a very subjective phenomenon based on the variation in severity for a 
      given degree of functional impairment. It is difficult to grade dyspnoea. 
      Dyspnoea is caused by a variety of physiological, pathophysiological, 
      psychological and environmental factors. The mechanisms leading to dyspnoea are 
      not completely understood. It is known that mechanical reasons like ventilation 
      disturbances (obstruction, restriction), impairment of the ventilation muscles, 
      skeletal deformation and many other reasons can cause dyspnoea. Every pulmonary 
      or cardiac disease may induce dyspnoea depending on the progression of the 
      underlying disease. The aim of this article is to give an overview of basic 
      pathophysiological mechanisms, diagnostic procedures and considerations with 
      regard to possible differential diagnoses.
