TI  - Palliation of tracheobronchial carcinoma: the role of cryosurgery.
PG  - 332, 334-6, 338-9
AB  - Bronchoscopy is a common day case procedure that can aid in the diagnosis and 
      treatment of tracheobronchial disorders. The controlled application of extreme 
      cold through a bronchoscope to endobronchial lesions (malignant and benign) is 
      known as endobronchial cryosurgery. This procedure improves respiratory function 
      and reduces shortness of breath and is performed in a cycle of three treatments. 
      This article describes the instrumentation required, how cryosurgery is performed 
      and how endobronchial cryosurgery can improve the patient's functional status and 
      survival.
