TI  - Basaloid squamous cell carcinoma of the lung: a rare tumour with a rare clinical 
      presentation.
PG  - 109-11
AB  - Basaloid squamous cell carcinoma of the lung, an uncommon subtype of non-small 
      cell carcinomas was introduced as a distinct entity in the recently revised World 
      Health Organization (WHO) classification of lung tumours. This rare tumour most 
      commonly develops in males older than 60 years. We report a 23-years-old female 
      patient with basaloid squamous cell carcinoma of the lung who was stage IIB 
      post-operatively. The patient is still alive and healthy 18 months after the 
      operation. This is one of the youngest patient reported with this rare type of 
      tumour.
