TI  - Transplantation in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease.
PG  - 149-62
AB  - Lung transplantation is a surgical option for patients who fail optimization of 
      medical treatment for the severe symptoms that result from COPD. This review will 
      discuss patient selection, transplant listing, and the surgical technique for 
      transplantation in COPD. Furthermore, it will describe transplant outcomes and 
      its effects on recipient survival, pulmonary function, exercise capacity, 
      respiratory muscle function, and quality of life. The respective roles of 
      transplantation and lung volume reduction surgery as therapies for advanced 
      disease will be outlined.
