TI  - Sleeve pneumonectomy.
PG  - 109-13
AB  - Throughout the last year significant advances in the operative technique and 
      management of patients undergoing sleeve pneumonectomy, as well as better 
      understanding of patient selection requirements, have led to improved 
      perioperative and long-term results. Patients with N2 disease resistant to 
      preoperative chemotherapy or chemo-/radiotherapy should be excluded from the 
      procedure. Airway resection should be limited to a maximum length of 4 cm. In 
      general sleeve pneumonectomy has become an established procedure for treatment of 
      lung cancer involving the carina and should be performed for carefully selected 
      patients in experienced centers only.
