TI  - [Unusual foreign body aspiration].
PG  - 288-91
AB  - Tracheobronchial foreign body aspiration in adults is rare when compared to 
      children. In this case report, 76 year old female patient who aspirated a screw 
      of tracheostomy cannula which was taken out by fiberoptic bronchoscopy (FOB) was 
      presented. This case showed us that education of patients about stoma care is 
      important. The FOB can be used safely to get foreign body from distal airways.
