PMID- 16704045
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20060928
LR  - 20211203
IS  - 1027-3719 (Print)
IS  - 1027-3719 (Linking)
VI  - 10
IP  - 5
DP  - 2006 May
TI  - Tuberculosis and granuloma formation in patients receiving anti-TNF therapy.
PG  - 588-90
AB  - In patients receiving anti-tumor necrosis factor (TNF) therapy, a probable 
      exacerbation of latent tuberculosis (TB) is a major adverse event. The impairment 
      of granuloma differentiation is considered a characteristic feature of TB in 
      these patients. In this report we present three patients with rheumatic disease 
      who developed TB under infliximab treatment. All of them had typical granulomas 
      on the biopsy specimens, indicating that the expected impairment of granuloma 
      formation is not always the case. The notion of granuloma-free TB in patients 
      receiving anti-TNF therapy could shift a clinician's path away from performing a 
      biopsy, thus delaying the establishment of a correct diagnosis.
