DP  - 2006 Mar
TI  - Collapse of a new type of self-expanding metallic tracheal stent.
PG  - 56-8
AB  - Alveolus TB-STS is a new self-expanding, completely polyurethane-covered, 
      metallic stent which has been designed to be successfully used even in the 
      treatment of non-neoplastic airway strictures as it is supposed to be removable. 
      We recently observed the collapse of an Alveolus tracheal stent, causing dyspnea 
      and hemopthysis, in a 63-yr-old female patient with post-intubation tracheal 
      stenosis. Such a complication, which to our knowledge has never been previously 
      reported with metallic stent use, forced us to remove the stent.
