TI  - Lobar torsion after pulmonary resection; report of two cases.
PG  - 63-5
AB  - Lobar torsion is a rare complication after pulmonary resection. We report a case 
      of right middle lobe torsion following a right upper lobectomy, and left lower 
      lobe torsion following a left upper lobectomy. Careful postoperative clinical 
      observation, chest radiography, fiberoptic bronchoscopy (FOB), and computed 
      tomography (CT) are crucial for precise diagnosis of lobar torsion following 
      pulmonary resection. Both patients underwent re-thoracotomy; a middle lobectomy 
      and completion pneumonectomy were performed. In the clinical management of lobar 
      torsion urgent diagnosis and conclusive surgical resection is needed to avoid 
      mortality and morbidity.
