TI  - Ectopic thymoma simulating a pericardial cyst.
PG  - 230-3
AB  - We present a case of a 53 year old man with a thymoma near the pericardium, a 
      rare ectopic localisation of thymoma. A round radiodensity found at the right 
      cardiophrenic angle was initially suspected at the echocardiography to be a 
      pericardial cyst. The diagnosis of thymoma was made only after histopathological 
      examination of the surgically re-sected lesion.
