TI  - [Cryorecanalization of an endobronchial lipoma].
PG  - 685-8
AB  - In this case presentation the advantages of a new method of cryoextraction of an 
      endobronchial lipoma are demonstrated. With an improved probe with high 
      mechanical stability large areas of the lipoma can be frozen and removed from the 
      bronchial wall. The tissue is directly extracted from the tumor. 
      Cryorecanalization permits during one procedure the reopening of an endoluminal 
      airway obstruction.
