TI  - Off pump coronary artery bypass grafting in a patient with tracheopathia 
      osteoplastica.
PG  - 495-6
AB  - Tracheopathia osteoplastica is a rare disease of the tracheobronchial tree, which 
      is often misdiagnosed and recognised only at post-mortem. We report the case of a 
      66-year-old man with this condition, mistakenly thought to be suffering from 
      chronic bronchiectasis. He underwent successful coronary artery bypass grafting 
      for unstable angina using an off-pump technique. A case report and brief 
      literature review is presented.
