TI  - [The endoscopic treatment of bronchial fistulas by submucosal injections].
PG  - 38-41
AB  - A total of 21 patients (aged 30-72) with bronchial stump fistulas (307 mm) were 
      treated by a newly developed method of treatment of purulent-destructive 
      pulmonary diseases. This technique represents a gradual narrowing of the 
      bronchial fistula lumen due to infiltrate formation in the submucosal bronchial 
      layer. The volume formation substance biopolymer "DAM+", hydrogenous biopolymer 
      with ions of silver "Argiform" for endoprosthesis of the soft tissues, is 
      injected into the submucosal bronchial layer. It is necessary to make 5-20 
      fibrobronchoscopies for bronchial fistula healing. No complications occurred as a 
      result of this treatment. The healing of bronchial fistula and bronchial stump 
      epithelization were found in 18 patients.
