TI  - Foggy vision.
PG  - 285-9
AB  - A 53-year-old man with history of "foggy vision" was referred for 
      neuro-ophthalmic consultation. His examination showed a right homonymous 
      hemianopia detected with automated perimetry. Brain magnetic resonance imaging 
      showed extensive enhancement of the structures in the sellar region and patchy 
      meningeal enhancement. Blood workup was unremarkable. He eventually had 
      bronchoscopy, which confirmed the diagnosis of sarcoidosis.
