TI  - Congenital lobar emphysema: an otolaryngologic perspective.
PG  - 549-54
AB  - Congenital lobar emphysema (CLE) is an uncommon but potentially life threatening 
      pulmonary abnormality affecting infants. Patients often present within the first 
      6 months of life with recurrent respiratory distress as a result of 
      hyperinflation of the affected pulmonary lobe, and resultant near total collapse 
      of normal lung parenchyma. We present a case of a 2-month-old infant with 
      recurrent admissions for respiratory distress.
