TI  - Case report: a ball valve blood clot in the airways - life-saving whole tube 
      suction.
PG  - R289-90
AB  - Respiratory tract obstruction due to a blood clot may result in life threatening 
      ventilatory impairment. Ball valve blood clot obstructions of the airways are 
      rare. A ball valve blood clot acts as a one-way valve, allowing (near) normal air 
      entry into the airways, but (completely) blocking expiration. In a near fatal 
      case of obstruction of the airways by a ball valve blood clot, we performed 
      'whole tube suction' to resolve the airway problem.
