TI  - [Approach of diffuse interstitial lung diseases].
PG  - 285-99
AB  - Diffuse interstitial lung diseases (DILD) are heterogeneous set of diseases 
      affecting the interstitium of the lung. The etiologic factors may be known or 
      unknown. The diagnosis is based on the disease history, findings of the physical 
      and radiological examinations, physiological and bronchoscopic findings, the 
      cyto- and/or histopathological findings of the bronchoscopic materials and 
      surgical lung biopsy in some selected patients. The reader will find the 
      definition, classification, general properties and clinical approach of DILD.
