TI  - Transient phrenic nerve paralysis associated with status asthmaticus.
PG  - 269-71
AB  - Phrenic nerve paralysis is a condition typically occurring after invasive 
      procedures in the chest and neck. Here we describe a case of transient unilateral 
      diaphragmatic paralysis in a child with status asthmaticus complicated by 
      complete right lung atelectasis. Common causes of this disorder and possible 
      implications for our case are discussed.
