DP  - 2003 Dec
TI  - Two cases of endobronchial neurilemmoma and review of the literature in Japan.
PG  - 1215-8
AB  - Neurilemmomas are benign tumors which originate from Schwann cells. They rarely 
      occur in the trachea or bronchus. We encountered two cases of endobronchial 
      neurilemmoma and in this context, reviewed 48 cases previously reported in Japan. 
      Neurilemmomas can occur in all regions of the bronchial tree and they often 
      progress into both intraluminal and extraluminal spaces. Incomplete resection 
      results in a local recurrence, despite being rare. As for appropriate therapies, 
      surgery, bronchofiberoptic removal and yttrium aluminum garnet (YAG) laser 
      resection can be chosen depending on the patient's status.
