TI  - Postobstructive pulmonary oedema during anaesthesia in children with 
      mucopolysaccharidoses.
PG  - 441-7
AB  - We present case reports of five patients with severe forms of 
      mucopolysaccharidoses who developed postobstructive pulmonary oedema during 
      anaesthesia. The difficulties of anaesthesia in these patients and the particular 
      predisposition that these patients exhibit for the development of postobstructive 
      pulmonary oedema is discussed.
