TI  - The burned trachea.
PG  - 343-8
AB  - Tracheal burns caused by thermal or chemical injuries are uncommon, but they can 
      be difficult to manage. A high index of suspicion is required for early detection 
      of these injuries. Acutely, they are often life threatening unless they are 
      diagnosed quickly and managed properly. Tracheal burn injuries can lead to 
      long-term stenoses, which require specialized surgical techniques and chronic 
      therapy--often with Montgomery T-tubes--for their proper management.
