TI  - Pediatric tracheal surgery.
PG  - 305-14, vii
AB  - Pediatric tracheal surgery is uncommon, and few centers have enough experience to 
      make meaningful conclusions about treatment. Short-segment congenital tracheal 
      stenosis is treated by tracheal resection, whereas long-segment stenosis is 
      treated by either augmentation tracheoplasty or slide tracheoplasty (the author's 
      preferred approach). Tracheomalacia is treated most commonly by aortopexy. 
      Postintubation tracheal stenosis is usually treated by tracheal (or 
      laryngotracheal) resection.
