TI  - Chronic lobar consolidation.
PG  - 112-4
AB  - Lobar consolidation in a chest X-ray is often thought to be due to infection. We 
      present the problem of a 66-year-old female with low grade non-Hodgkin's lymphoma 
      of the mucosa associated lymphoid tissue (MALT) type who had features of lobar 
      consolidation that persisted for years. The different causes, both infectious and 
      non-infectious, of this kind of presentation are discussed.
