TI  - The solitary pulmonary nodule.
PG  - 89S-96S
AB  - More than 150,00 patients a year present to their physicians with the diagnostic 
      dilemma of a solitary pulmonary nodule (SPN) found either on chest radiography or 
      chest CT. A thoughtful and timely workup of this finding is essential if lung 
      cancer is to be recognized early and the chance for cure optimized. Based on the 
      literature to date, recommendations are made for appropriate imaging modalities 
      and diagnostic testing, as well as indications for obtaining preoperative tissue 
      diagnosis for the patient with an SPN.
