TI  - Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis.
PG  - 260-3
AB  - A 23-year-old man was admitted to the hospital because of dyspnea. Chest X-ray 
      showed reticulo-nodular opacities. The crazy paving appearance on high-resolution 
      CT was highly suggestive of pulmonary alveolar proteinosis. Histologic 
      examination confirmed the diagnosis. Pulmonary alveolar proteinosis is a rare 
      disease but an important diagnosis to make as treatment with pulmonary lavage is 
      curative in a large proportion of patients.
