TI  - Colonic metastasis from bronchogenic carcinoma presenting as pancolitis.
PG  - 199-200
AB  - The colonic metastases from bronchogenic carcinoma are rare. We present a 
      73-year-old man presented with features suggestive of pan colitis after 
      metastasis from undifferentiated large cell carcinoma of the lung. The plain 
      radiograph and computed tomography scan of the chest had revealed a mass lesion 
      in the right lower lobe of lung. He had no evidence of significant lesions 
      elsewhere. Considering the advanced stage and poor differentiation of the tumour, 
      no active therapy was undertaken and he survived for three months.
