TI  - Spontaneous breathing combined with high frequency ventilation during 
      bronchoscopic resection of a large tracheal tumour.
PG  - 641-3
AB  - A patient with learning difficulties had a large tracheal tumour at the carina 
      that caused severe respiratory distress. I.v. anaesthesia with propofol, 
      spontaneous breathing through a tracheal tube, and high frequency jet ventilation 
      were successfully employed during bronchoscopic resection of the tumour.
