TI  - Unusual cause of chronic cough in a four-year-old cured by uvulectomy.
PG  - 144-6
AB  - A 4-year-old boy had a history of persistent barking cough unresponsive to 
      medical treatment since infancy. He described a feeling of something in his 
      throat. When investigated by flexible fiberoptic bronchoscopy, the only 
      abnormality was the uvula resting in contact with the epiglottis. The cough was 
      no longer present after uvulectomy.
