TI  - Tracheal stenosis caused by false aneurysm of the right subclavian artery.
PG  - 946-7
AB  - The development of tracheal stenosis following insertion of a central venous 
      catheter is a rare complication of this procedure. We present the case of an 
      81-year-old woman, who suffered acute onset of dyspnea, stridor and dysphagia 4 
      weeks after coronary artery bypass surgery. Investigations revealed a false 
      aneurysm of the right subclavian artery, compressing the trachea and the 
      oesophagus. The iatrogenic lesion was caused by the insertion of a central venous 
      catheter via the right subclavian route. By the time symptoms developed the 
      catheter had already been removed.
