TI  - Tracheobronchopathia osteoplastica: incidental finding at tracheal intubation.
PG  - 515-7
AB  - Subglottic papillomatous growths were observed on routine tracheal intubation for 
      a scheduled colorectal procedure. Fibreoptic bronchoscopy revealed that the 
      lesions extended down to the carina and into the main bronchi. The diagnosis of 
      tracheobronchopathia osteoplastica was made after subsequent bronchoscopy and 
      biopsy in the post-operative period. A brief review of this rare benign condition 
      is given.
