VI  - 45
IP  - 2
DP  - 2001 May
TI  - Fatal cerebral air embolism as a complication of transbronchoscopic lung biopsy: 
      a case report.
PG  - 215-7
AB  - A rare complication of transbronchoscopic lung biopsy, namely a cerebral air 
      embolism, is presented. The course of events following the embolic episode in the 
      form of a fall in blood pressure, bradycardia and convulsions is documented, as 
      is the presence of an air emboli on the CT scan of the brain with subsequent 
      resorption of the emboli on the follow-up scan. The salient features of the case 
      are the rarity of the complication and the excellent temporal depiction of 
      imaging findings on CT scan demonstrated as resorption of air emboli and 
      subsequent watershed territory infarcts.
