TI  - A pin in the neck.
PG  - 20
AB  - We report a unique case of a 40 year old female who presented with recurrent open 
      safety pin aspiration. She had a long history of personality disorder and 
      self-inflicted injury. On two occasions the open pin was removed with the aid of 
      rigid bronchoscopy. However on one occasion a tracheostomy was required for 
      removal of the safety pin.
