TI  - Mucus plugging as a cause of acute lobar overdistension.
PG  - 38-9
AB  - Acute lobar overdistension in children is usually indicative of foreign body 
      aspiration, especially when a history of a choking episode is recalled. An 
      unusual presentation of asthma as recurrent overdistension of the left lung in a 
      toddler is described. The child had undergone two consecutive negative 
      bronchoscopies with a presumptive diagnosis of foreign body aspiration; however, 
      it was only the antiasthmatic treatment that resulted in an excellent outcome.
