TI  - Compression of the trachea by the innominate artery in a 2-month-old child.
PG  - 80-5
AB  - SUMMARY. We utilized improved methods for assessing airway structure and function 
      to define the clinical significance of the innominate artery syndrome. Both 
      infant pulmonary function tests (IPFT) and noninvasive controlled ventilation 
      computed tomography (CVCT) were used, along with traditional diagnostic 
      techniques in a 2-month-old child with compression of the trachea by the 
      innominate artery. These tests provided objective documentation of functional 
      impairment before surgery and improvement postoperatively. These tests should aid 
      in the understanding of this controversial syndrome and help to further define 
      treatment options.
