TI  - Spontaneous coughing up of a polyp.
PG  - 101-3
AB  - We report the case of an 18-year old female with right lower lobe atelectasis, 
      who was admitted to our hospital because of a nonproductive cough. She underwent 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy that revealed a peduncular polyp in the right truncus 
      intermedius or middle bronchus. Before admission for laser polypectomy, she 
      spontaneously coughed up the tissue mass, and the right lower lobe atelectasis 
      disappeared. We report a rare case of 'autopolypectomy' of a bronchial adenoma.
